      "content": "Various mathematical and statistical packages provide routines for computing cumulative probabilities of noncentral $ \\chi^{2} $ and F random variables, and a number of approximations have been suggested (e.g., Patnaik 1949, Severo and Zelen 1960, Tiku 1965). Winer et al. (1991) offer one such approximation based on the unit normal U, with the probability that a noncentral F-distributed random variable exceeds a value $ F_{0} $ being approximately",
